  "content": {
    "id": "p14-q13-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "13",
    "prompt": "Find the dimensions of a rectangle whose area is $2\\text{ m}^2$ and whose perimeter is $8\\text{ m}$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$(2-\\sqrt2)\\text{ m}$ by $(2+\\sqrt2)\\text{ m}$.",
      "worked": "Let the dimensions be $x$ metres and $y$ metres.\n$$\\begin{align*}2(x+y)&=8\\\\x+y&=4\\\\y&=4-x\\\\x(4-x)&=2\\\\x^2-4x&=-2\\\\x^2-4x+4&=-2+4\\\\(x-2)^2&=2\\\\x&=2\\pm\\sqrt2.\\end{align*}$$\nThe dimensions are $(2-\\sqrt2)\\text{ m}$ and $(2+\\sqrt2)\\text{ m}$. Both are positive; their sum is $4\\text{ m}$ and their product is $2\\text{ m}^2$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 92
  },
